<main><section class="page-hero section-shell"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PROJECT</span><h1>Building a small OS with a big systems surface.</h1><p>NotYVOS explores what it takes to build an x86-64 operating system from boot to desktop, while also providing a foundation for PlayStation 3 runtime experimentation.</p></section>
<section class="section-shell section"><div class="prose-grid"><article class="prose reveal"><h2>The idea</h2><p>NotYVOS is a freestanding x86-64 operating system with a native kernel, userland, VFS, persistent NYFS storage, software-rendered desktop and hardware drivers. It is developed as a real systems project rather than a themed shell over another operating system.</p><p>The project also contains a PS3 runtime foundation with PowerPC execution, SPU, DMA, JIT and RSX compatibility components. These areas are developed as separate runtime domains inside the wider system.</p><h2>Project philosophy</h2><ul><li>Keep architecture understandable and documented.</li><li>Prefer native components where practical.</li><li>Make subsystem boundaries explicit.</li><li>Document limitations instead of hiding incomplete areas.</li><li>Keep third-party components attributed and separated.</li></ul></article><aside class="side-card reveal"><span class="eyebrow">PLATFORM</span><dl><div><dt>CPU</dt><dd>x86-64</dd></div><div><dt>Kernel</dt><dd>C++20</dd></div><div><dt>Userland</dt><dd>C17</dd></div><div><dt>Boot</dt><dd>Limine v12.9.0</dd></div><div><dt>Build</dt><dd>CMake + Ninja</dd></div><div><dt>License</dt><dd>AGPL-3.0-or-later</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
<section class="section-shell section tinted"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">BOUNDARIES</span><h2>What it does not claim</h2></div><div class="card-grid three"><article class="feature-card"><h3>Not Windows</h3><p>Windows PE/Win32 compatibility is explicitly excluded from the current roadmap.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><h3>Not PS3 firmware</h3><p>PS3 firmware is user-supplied and remains isolated from the native firmware direction.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><h3>Not finished</h3><p>NotYVOS remains a development-stage operating system with substantial queued work.</p></article></div></section></main><?php require __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php'; ?>